<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReadingInterharmonic.numerator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReadingInterharmonic> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReadingInterharmonic.numerator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReadingInterharmonic.numerator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Interharmonic numerator. Value 0 means not applicable. Value 1 is used in combination with denominator2 to represent interharmonic 12 and with denominator1 it represents fundamental frequency. Finally values greater than 1 indicate the harmonic of that order e.g. numerator5 is the fifth harmonic." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ReadingInterharmonic.numerator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "numerator"@en .
