<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingControl.targetDeadband> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "This is a deadband used with discrete control to avoid excessive update of controls like tap changers and shunt compensator banks while regulating.  The units of those appropriate for the mode. The attribute shall be a positive value or zero. If RegulatingControl.discrete is set to false the RegulatingControl.targetDeadband is to be ignored.Note that for instance if the targetValue is 100 kV and the targetDeadband is 2 kV the range is from 99 to 101 kV." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#RegulatingControl.targetDeadband> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "targetDeadband"@en .
# 
