<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePoint.isVirtual> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "If true this usage point is virtual i.e. no physical location exists in the network where a meter could be located to collect the meter readings. For example one may define a virtual usage point to serve as an aggregation of usage for all of a companys premises distributed widely across the distribution territory. Otherwise the usage point is physical i.e. there is a logical point in the network where a meter could be located to collect meter readings." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#UsagePoint.isVirtual> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "isVirtual"@en .
# 
