<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConditionFactorKind> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConditionFactorKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Enumeration> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConditionFactorKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Kind of condition factor." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConditionFactorKind> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ConditionFactorKind"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductance
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#CIMDatatype> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Factor by which voltage must be multiplied to give corresponding power lost from a circuit. Real part of admittance." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Conductance"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductancePerLength
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductancePerLength> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductancePerLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#CIMDatatype> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductancePerLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Real part of admittance per unit of length." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductancePerLength> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ConductancePerLength"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductingEquipment
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductingEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductingEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Equipment> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductingEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The parts of the AC power system that are designed to carry current or that are conductively connected through terminals." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductingEquipment> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ConductingEquipment"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductor
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConductingEquipment> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Combination of conducting material with consistent electrical characteristics building a single electrical system used to carry current between points in the power system.  " .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Conductor> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Conductor"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConfigurationEvent
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConfigurationEvent> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConfigurationEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ActivityRecord> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConfigurationEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Used to report details on creation change or deletion of an entity or its configuration." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConfigurationEvent> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ConfigurationEvent"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConformLoad
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConformLoad> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConformLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EnergyConsumer> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConformLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "ConformLoad represent loads that follow a daily load change pattern where the pattern can be used to scale the load with a system load." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConformLoad> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "ConformLoad"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ConformLoadGroup
