<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#DiscExcContIEEEDEC3A> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#DiscontinuousExcitationControlDynamics> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#DiscExcContIEEEDEC3A> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "IEEE type DEC3A model. In some systems the stabilizer output is disconnected from the regulator immediately following a severe fault to prevent the stabilizer from competing with action of voltage regulator during the first swing.Reference IEEE 421.52005 12.4. " .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#DiscExcContIEEEDEC3A> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "DiscExcContIEEEDEC3A"@en .
