<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IntervalReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Data captured at regular intervals of time. Interval data could be captured as incremental data absolute data or relative data. The source for the data is usually a tariff quantity or an engineering quantity. Data is typically captured in timetagged uniform fixedlength intervals of 5 min 10 min 15 min 30 min or 60 min.Note Interval Data is sometimes also called Interval Data Readings IDR." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IntervalReading> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "IntervalReading"@en .
