# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Limit
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Limit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Limit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Limit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specifies one limit value for a Measurement. A Measurement typically has several limits that are kept together by the LimitSet class. The actual meaning and use of a Limit instance i.e. if it is an alarm or warning limit or if it is a high or low limit is not captured in the Limit class. However the name of a Limit instance may indicate both meaning and use." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Limit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Limit"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitDependency
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitDependency> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitDependency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitDependency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A limit calculation model used to compute an operational limit based on external input such as temperature. These are intended to be shared among operational limits with the same calculation form that apply to a piece of equipment.." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitDependency> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LimitDependency"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitScalingLimit
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitScalingLimit> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitScalingLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitDependency> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitScalingLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specifies an operational  limit is calculated by scaling another operational limit." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitScalingLimit> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LimitScalingLimit"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitSet
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitSet> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitSet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#IdentifiedObject> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitSet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Specifies a set of Limits that are associated with a Measurement. A Measurement may have several LimitSets corresponding to seasonal or other changing conditions. The condition is captured in the name and description attributes. The same LimitSet may be used for several Measurements. In particular percentage limits are used this way." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LimitSet> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LimitSet"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Line
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Line> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Line> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EquipmentContainer> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Line> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Contains equipment beyond a substation belonging to a power transmission line. " .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Line> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Line"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineDetail
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineDetail> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineDetail> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Compound> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineDetail> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Details on an amount line with rounding date and note." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineDetail> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LineDetail"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineFault
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineFault> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineFault> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#Fault> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineFault> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A fault that occurs on an AC line segment at some point along the length." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LineFault> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LineFault"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensator
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensator> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
