<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A linear shunt compensator has banks or sections with equal admittance values." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensator> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LinearShuntCompensator"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensatorPhase
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensatorPhase> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensatorPhase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ShuntCompensatorPhase> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensatorPhase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A per phase linear shunt compensator has banks or sections with equal admittance values." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LinearShuntCompensatorPhase> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LinearShuntCompensatorPhase"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregate
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregate> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadDynamics> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Aggregate loads are used to represent all or part of the real and reactive load from one or more loads in the static power flow data. This load is usually the aggregation of many individual load devices and the load model is an approximate representation of the aggregate response of the load devices to system disturbances.Standard aggregate load model comprised of static andor dynamic components.  A static load model represents the sensitivity of the real and reactive power consumed by the load to the amplitude and frequency of the bus voltage. A dynamic load model can be used to represent the aggregate response of the motor components of the load." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LoadAggregate"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregationPoint
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#AggregateNode> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A specialized class of type AggregatedNode type. Defines Load Aggregation Points." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadAggregationPoint> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LoadAggregationPoint"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadArea
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadArea> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadArea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#EnergyArea> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadArea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The class is the root or first level in a hierarchical structure for grouping of loads for the purpose of load flow load scaling." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadArea> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LoadArea"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBid
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBid> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ResourceBid> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Offer to supply energyancillary services from a load resource participating load reduces consumption." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBid> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LoadBid"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBreakSwitch
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBreakSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBreakSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#ProtectedSwitch> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBreakSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A mechanical switching device capable of making carrying and breaking currents under normal operating conditions." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadBreakSwitch> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LoadBreakSwitch"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadComposite
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadComposite> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadDynamics> .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Combined static load and induction motor load effects.The dynamics of the motor are simplified by linearizing the induction machine equations." .
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadComposite> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "LoadComposite"@en .
# 
# http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadDistributionFactor
<http://www.iec.ch/TC57/CIM#LoadDistributionFactor> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
